# Without this, actions/checkout on Windows checks these out with CRLF
# line endings (Git for Windows' core.autocrlf=true default) — patches
# authored on Linux/macOS are LF-only, so git apply's context-line
# matching fails with "patch does not apply" even though the diff
# content itself is correct (a real windows-x64 CI failure this fixed).
# Shell scripts pinned the same way since Git Bash tolerates CRLF
# inconsistently depending on the construct.
*.patch text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
